  "N22" [label="(13,0,0) Currently there is: CVD is more flexible but its large-scale application is extremely restricted by high energy intensity, limited product types and low yield."];
  "N23" [label="(0,0,0) If a synthesis method has high energy intensity, limited product types and low yield, then its large-scale application is extremely restricted."];
  "N28" [label="(17,0,0) Currently there is: The synthesis is restricted by the solution pH, solubility and hydrolysis of precursors."];
  "N3" [label="(3,0,0) Currently there is: 2D metal oxides are a large family with unique combinations of redox chemistry, abundant defect sites, rapid mass transport and high earth abundance, endowing them with widespread applications."];
  "N30" [label="(0,0,0) If the synthesis process is restricted by solution pH/solubility/hydrolysis of precursors, then it is limited for violent or refractory precursors."];
  "N37" [label="(21,0,0) Currently there is: Confinement synthesis in a fixed interlayer is the transverse growth of 2D target guest species by utilizing the layer spacing of lamellar framework in combination with template."];
