  "N4" [label="(0,0,0) If a solid has constrained longitudinal dimensionality, then it has unique properties and promising applications compared to bulk solids."];
  "N40" [label="(23,0,0) Observed phenomenon: Guo’s group reported the solution preparation of free-standing nitrogen-doped amorphous monolayer carbon within the interlayer cavity of LDHs, indicating the feasibility of confined polymerization using solid templates."];
  "N41" [label="(0,0,0) Knowledge: Feasibility of confined polymerization using solid templates can be adapted to metal oxides under dry-chemical melt infiltration to avoid liquid-phase hydrolysis issues."];
  "N42" [label="(0,0,0) abduction-reasoning: Given observed phenomenon of confined carbon synthesis in LDHs, and knowledge that it can be adapted for MOs with melt infiltration, therefore confined interlayer growth is feasible for various ultrathin 2D metal oxides."];
  "N43" [label="(0,0,0) General pattern: Existing top-down/bottom-up synthesis methods for 2D metal oxides suffer from limitations in scalability, versatility, applicability to non-layered materials, and precursor compatibility."];
