  "N8" [label="(4,0,0) Currently there is: Mechanical/chemical/ultrasonic exfoliation, CVD, template method, solvo-/hydrothermal methods etc. have been used to fabricate novel 2D architectures."];
  "N9" [label="(0,0,0) General pattern: A variety of top-down and bottom-up strategies have been developed for fabricating 2D materials."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) The paper proposes to develop and evaluate a dry-chemical strategy in which molten metal precursors infiltrate the fixed interlayer spaces of RUB-15 and undergo confined growth to yield monolayer 2D metal oxide nanosheets, extendable to sulfide nanosheets, with defect-rich surfaces and superior catalytic performance, thereby addressing limitations of conventional exfoliation and wet-chemical synthesis routes.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) The retained and repaired conclusions jointly establish that 2D metal oxides are scientifically valuable, conventional exfoliation, CVD, and wet-chemical synthesis routes have important constraints, and fixed interlayer confinement with dry melt infiltration offers a plausible route to dimension-limited ultrathin growth."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) Because CVD has high energy intensity, limited product types, and low yield, its large-scale application for 2D metal oxide synthesis is extremely restricted."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Because wet-chemical synthesis is restricted by solution pH, precursor solubility, and hydrolysis, it is limited for violent or refractory precursors."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) Combining melt infiltration with fixed interlayer confinement under dry-chemical conditions is a plausible strategy for dimension-limited growth of ultrathin 2D metal oxides."];
  "R3" [label="(0,0,0) A variety of top-down and bottom-up fabrication strategies have been developed for 2D materials and related 2D architectures."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) Confinement synthesis in a fixed interlayer can strictly limit the longitudinal dimension of target products according to the template layer spacing."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Documented limitations of exfoliation, CVD, and wet-chemical routes motivate the search for a more versatile and facile method to fabricate 2D metal oxide crystals."];
